TDISK                                                     (VM/370plus) CMS EXEC
Use the TDISK command to get a temporary disk (TDISK) in one step: CP
defines it, CMS formats it and, if you give a file mode, accesses it.
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
| TDISK    | [cyls] [fm]                                                      |
+----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+
cyls     the size in 3350 cylinders, 1 to 100.  The default is 10 (about
         5 MB).
fm       the file mode to access the disk as.  Without it the disk is
         formatted but not accessed; ACCESS it later yourself.
The two operands may be given in either order.

The disk gets the first free virtual address from D00 to D1F and the label
TMPvaddr.  Its contents are lost when you log off or DETACH it.

Examples
   TDISK              10 cylinders, formatted, not accessed
   TDISK T            10 cylinders, accessed as T
   TDISK 30 T         30 cylinders, accessed as T
   TDISK 5            5 cylinders, not accessed

Return codes
   0    the disk is ready
   24   invalid operands
   28   a disk is already accessed with that file mode
   32   no free virtual address, or no TEMP space for that size
   other  FORMAT's return code (the disk stays defined)
